WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:06.940
If you go on Lyft's website right now, it says drivers can make $35 per hour.  Is that realistic?

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.140
A few weeks ago, I spent a week
 driving for Lyft to find out.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:18.000
All right, it is 12:30, and I'm logging in to my Lyft App
to start my first Lyft job of the day.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.900
Driver mode is on. 
And, so far nothing is happening.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.660
I drove for 50 hours.  I had 54 passengers.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:30.100
And I made just under $600,
which works out to about 12 bucks an hour.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.900
And that's before subtracting the cost of gas.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.980
A big reason for my low earnings
was that I spent a lot of time waiting around.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.340
So with the traditional salaried position,
you work your 40 hours.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.920
And it's a company's job to make sure that you have enough work for it to be worth your salary.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.280
With this kind of business,
I, as an independent contractor, am on my own.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:52.720
I sit here for the next 5 or 6 or 7 hours,
and nobody wants a taxi ride, I'm just out of money.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:56.520
Like on Tuesday morning, I drove for about three hours and didn't get a single passenger,

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.120
and so that was pretty frustrating.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:03.880
So the day that one best was on Saturday. 
I worked about 10 hours, and I made 163 dollars,

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.360
after gas, it was about 14 dollars an hour.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.000
Why Saturday was my best day?

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.100
For one thing, I had passengers in my car 
35% of the time, a higher percentage than any other day.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.600
Second, four of my 14 rides had prime time bonuses,

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:20.800
where passengers are charged
a premium of 25% - 100%.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.820
Still, $14 an hour isn't great.
 And it's a lot less than the $35 Lyft is promoting.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:30.960
The fundamental issue is that right now at least,
the roads are crowded with people offering rides.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.140
Now that I'm looking around, I'm noticing
that I have a lot of competitors around me.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:39.540
That's partly because both Lyft and Uber
are aggressively recruiting drivers.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.020
While I only earned about $600 from customers,

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:46.440
Lyft was running a promotion in November
that guaranteed divers would make at least $30 an hour.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.480
So Lyft paid me another $900 out of their own pocket.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:56.180
As Uber and Lyft throw a lot of money at drivers to drive, it's expanding the number of drivers in the market.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:59.600
That means the drivers spend more time sitting around, and so, they actually make less.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.280
They need to grow quickly in order to compete with Uber, and so, I think they're spending a ton of money.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.360
They both have raised hundreds of
millions of dollars in venture capital,

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:09.840
and they're spending that
to build out their networks as quickly as possible,

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.800
and so, they're willing to spend a lot of money
in the short run to make sure that they're large as Uber,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.060
somebody who needs a steady paycheck,

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.420
this is probably not a good choice for you because we really don't know what the long-term future is gonna be,

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.100
and it's hard to predict from week to week.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.819
This isn't just something that people, 
do as a full-time job.

00:02:24.819 --> 00:02:27.729
There are a lot of people that do it
as a supplement to some other job.

00:02:27.729 --> 00:02:29.840
It can give employees a lot more freedom

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.260
because if I feel like, you know, not working later today
I can just take the day off and nobody cares.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.100
this model isn't for everyone, but for some people,
it's a great opportunity.

